  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening collective AAP mechanisms in Honduras</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of UNICEF project is to establish the first collective AAP mechanism in Honduras that guarantees the inclusion of affected population&#x2019;s perspectives in programmatic decision-making and promotes people&#x2019;s access to life-saving information. The project provides access to life-saving information, feedback and complaints about the experiences of the targeted people on humanitarian assistance through interaction with collective-interagency AAP mechanisms. The intervention provides humanitarian assistance to 111,250 people (46,721men,  39,031women and 25,488 children) including 1,112 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
